"q": "A company uses the AWS Glue Schema Registry with Apache Avro schemas for events on Amazon MSK. Producer teams always release schema changes first. Dozens of consumer applications owned by other teams upgrade on their own schedules, so at any time a consumer might be using any earlier schema version. Every consumer must be able to read data produced with the newest schema. Which compatibility mode meets this requirement while placing the fewest restrictions on schema changes?",
