"explanation": "Index State Management automates index lifecycles. You define states (for example hot → warm → delete) and the conditions for moving between them, such as index age. The `warm_migration` action moves an index to UltraWarm, which is read-only, S3-backed storage that costs much less per GB than hot storage and can still be searched. An ISM template attaches the policy to each new daily index automatically.",
