"q": "A gaming company is starting a new clickstream analytics workload. Amazon Data Firehose will write events into Apache Iceberg tables every minute, and analysts will query the tables from Amazon Athena and Amazon Redshift. There's no existing data to migrate. The platform team wants AWS to run all table maintenance, and it wants to grant access table by table without managing S3 prefix permissions.\n\nWhich solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
